-- title:
--   From HTo GAdjacent Stage Globalize Pointwise Shape
-- statement:
--   **Globalization of a pointwise type-sum identity.** Let `source` assign an error to a Boolean bit, a Boolean type pattern of length `n`, a slice height, and a point tuple. Let `target` assign an error to a slice height and point tuple. If, for every slice height $x$ and point tuple `xs`, the sum of `source` over the Boolean bit and type pattern equals `target`, then the corresponding sum of nested uniform averages equals the joint uniform average of `target`.
--   Write $\Theta$ for the parameter tuple and $F$ for the indexed family.
--   $$
--   \left(\forall x,xs,\ \sum_{b:\mathsf{Bool}}\sum_{\tau:\operatorname{GHatType}(n)}\operatorname{source}(b,\tau,x,xs)=\operatorname{target}(x,xs)\right)
--   \Longrightarrow
--   \sum_b\sum_\tau\mathbb E_x\mathbb E_{xs}\,\operatorname{source}(b,\tau,x,xs)
--   =\mathbb E_{(x,xs)\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q\times\operatorname{PointTuple}(\Theta,n))}\operatorname{target}(x,xs).
--   $$
--
--   The result exchanges finite sums with uniform averages and combines the two independent uniform distributions into their product distribution. It is the common averaging step used by the global A0, M1, M2, M3, and M4 adjacent-stage shape rewrites.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGAdjacentStage_globalize_pointwiseShape`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
